open-forge:
  description: Coordination for the four requested Neon Pairs regression fixes
  tags: [Memory, Working, Contextual]
---

# Game regressions

User requested all four fixes under docs/README.md, a plan before delegation, and a separate subagent per task. The parent must not edit code. Parent coordinates reviews and final verification.

Plan: best scores and missing-record display; keyboard board navigation; reduced motion; silent gameplay. Only one child can run at a time, so assignments are sequential. Each child owns its fix and focused checks. Full type, unit, build, browser and formatting checks follow integration.

Initial causes: rememberBest unconditionally overwrote scores; GameStatus used zero for missing best; board navigation handlers were absent; card and status styles lacked reduced-motion overrides; use-game.ts started Web Audio tones.

Scores are fixed by best_scores: storage.ts preserves equal/worse results, and GameStatus.tsx renders none for absent records. Seventeen focused tests and typecheck passed. Keyboard navigation is fixed in Board.tsx and use-board-focus.ts: plain arrow keys move within row/column, edges stop, and modifier combos are left alone. Existing browser journeys cover arrow movement, edge stops, focus visibility, paused snapshots and 16x16/zoom. Its React KeyboardEvent import is type-only and unaliased to satisfy source conventions. Task 2 passes npm run typecheck, npm run build, npm test and git diff --check. Reduced motion is fixed in card.css and status.css: media rules remove the card border transition and win banner pulse. Prettier and git diff --check pass for both stylesheets. Silence is fixed in use-game.ts: match and win Web Audio tones are removed while the shared activation and clock flow remains. Production source audit, targeted formatting, diff check and typecheck pass. The full Vitest suite now passes: 138 tests across 19 files. Locked npm ci succeeded under Node 26.12.1/npm 11.20.0. Chromium setup is being changed to the headless shell for verification.

Final verification is running in exec session 35879: PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH=/work/.playwright-browsers NEON_PAIRS_NAMED_COMBINATION=1 npm run test:e2e. The exact Chromium 156.0.8078.4 headless shell is installed. Final source diff reviewed and git diff --check passes. All changed files pass formatting; full format:check flags 17 pre-existing files in docs/framework/tests. Optional open-forge doctor crashes internally with ArgumentException; context and index work.

Browser verification: the full named Chromium run recorded 74 pass, no assertion failures, and one cancellation at 30.081s: the existing `tests/art.e2e.test.ts` 128-card silhouette screenshot exceeded its default 30s budget. Assigned this verification issue to browser_verification. It adds the existing 90s `TestTimeouts.long` only for this serial 128-image check; every one of the 128 silhouette comparisons and all screenshot artifacts remain unchanged. Isolated named test passes in 45.1s. Full npm test passes 138/138; typecheck, file-only Prettier and diff checks pass after this test-only change. The requested-feature browser journeys all passed in the full run.

Follow the loader and specification for every assignment. Use git -c safe.directory=/work for repository reads. Remove this temporary record at completion, then preview/apply open-forge index to remove its catalogue entry. Parent has edited only this coordination note; all source edits are by the four child agents.

